  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The machine as shown has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> rods of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> connected by a pivot at the top. The end of one rod is connected to the floor by a stationary pivot and the end of the other rod has roller that rolls along the floor in a slot. As the roller goes back and forth, a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> weight moves up and down. If the roller is moving towards right at a constant speed, the weight moves up with a :<br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0136_a047a4adcf0b.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 167px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Speed which is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math> of that of the roller when the weight is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> above the ground",
      "is_correct": false
